WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.543
You're getting subway juice on you.

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:03.003
- That's very New York.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:03.670
- Yeah, I know.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:07.465
- So we're heading down to Williamsburg
for lunch, taking the subway down there.

00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:10.427
On the way down, we're gonna get in a quick
game of Truth or Dare, have a little fun—

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:10.969
- Beautiful.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:12.012
- With some New Yorkers here.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.101
- Truth or dare?

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:18.685
- Truth.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.646
- Your first at-bat this year came against Max Scherzer.
- Yeah.

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:23.523
- Chased a slider, first pitch.
- Yep.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.858
- What's going through
your head at that point?

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.652
- Well, I just wanted to get
the first hit out of the way.

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.070
It was kinda just like, "Oh, wow.

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:29.779
I'm here."

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:31.948
Took a big rip with that,
with that first swing.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:36.953
It's like, "Hey, Max Scherzer did what Max
Scherzer does by making it not be there."

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:39.164
Thankfully I got first one
out of the way my last at-bat.

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:42.375
- [Announcer]: Looped into center
field, that's gonna fall for a base hit.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.586
Pete Alonso with his first big league hit.

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:46.379
- We'll go to another truth.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.256
What's the scouting report
on Tebow the baseball player?

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.092
- I'm not gonna give it away
because he's a former teammate.

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:53.887
I don't want to give away his
thing, but I'll give you a fun fact.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:56.181
He does not believe in the baseball gods.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:01:00.185
- How does that play out for him versus most
people who do believe in the baseball gods?

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:04.272
- Guys that have been in the game for a
while, it's like they know the baseball gods

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:04.939
are a thing.

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.567
Our shortstop made this
unbelievable diving catch.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.361
I said something like, "Oh, baseball
gods," or something about it.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:11.988
It's like, "They're gonna do him right."

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.616
And he's like, "What the
hell are you talking about?"

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.284
Or, "What the heaven are you talking about?"

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:17.660
because it's Tim talking.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.244
Next pitch.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.498
he whacks a double off the wall, and
I just kinda look at him and smile.

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:23.083
He didn't talk to me for the rest of the day.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.209
- He's got the football gods.

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:25.543
- Nope.

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:27.712
No football gods.

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:28.463
- All right, Pete.

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:29.756
Truth or dare on this stop?

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:30.799
- I'll do a dare.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.842
- I've heard you have a
pretty good New York accent.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:37.514
So the dare is, I want you to approach
someone on the subway and ask for directions

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:40.809
to Citi Field with this great New
York accent that I've heard about.

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:41.184
- I gotta get

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:41.267
--
All

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:44.437
right.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.355
Hey, excuse me, sir.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.731
Can you do me a huge favor?

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:50.193
Can you give me directions to Citi Field?

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:52.821
Cuz I don't know if I'm in
the right direction or not.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:53.738
- You see my hat?

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.698
- I don't care if you're a fan or not.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.575
I just need directions to Citi Field.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.535
- I don't care, bro.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.286
This is New York, man.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:01.704
Figure it out.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.374
- Just please out of the
kindness of your heart.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:05.416
- Gimme money.

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:07.085
- Money?!

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:07.502
- Yeah, bro.

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:08.086
- Money?!

00:02:08.086 --> 00:02:09.838
Money?!

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:15.343
- What do you wanna do, truth or dare?  

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:18.513
- I just did a dare, so I'll just do, I'll do a truth to mix it up a little bit. 

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.807
- All right. Can you outlift everybody on the Mets? 

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:25.186
- Probably not. I mean, Noah gets after it. I mean, Buffalo's a really large human being.

00:02:25.186 --> 00:02:29.149
I mean, I can move some weight around for sure. But if anyone, probably Buffalo. 

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.108
- Yeah? 

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.527
- I'll put this in there: Noah bruises like a peach.  

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.865
- We got a little bit of time, got
another chance for a truth or dare.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:37.323
What you wanna do?

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:38.783
- I'll do a dare.

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:40.410
- I was hoping you'd say that.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.954
You know, you're kind of
a new star in New York.

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:47.167
The dare will be complete when you give them
your autograph and when you get them to sign

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:48.418
